        <briefdescription>
<para>Maximum number of schedule changes (create/update/patch/delete) permitted per interval window. 0 means disabled (no limit). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>When &gt; 0 the orchestrator tracks mutations per schedule per rolling interval. Excess mutations are rejected with <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1maintenance_1ae1a42412965993222bd7e6ca427ee05ba89eb04a7d77d4cd399ea2e4ee8cbd63e" kindref="member">MaintenanceError::kChurnLimitExceeded</ref>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The interval duration is controlled by DatabaseMaintenanceOrchestrator::kChurnIntervalMs (default 60 s). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
